I am building a learning platform similar to KodeKloud that teaches Git and Docker through tutorials and interactive labs.

The project stack is:

Frontend: react.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
Authentication: Firebase Authentication
Backend: FastAPI
Database: Firebase Firestore (for now)
Labs will be implemented later.

I already have an existing FastAPI backend that correctly implements Firebase Authentication by verifying Firebase ID tokens using the Firebase Admin SDK. I will provide this backend only as a reference for the authentication flow. Do not copy unrelated backend code. Only study how authentication and authorization are implemented.
Your task is to build the frontend authentication module from scratch.

Requirements:

Use Firebase Authentication client SDK.
Store Firebase configuration using environment variables.
Implement Login, Register and Logout.
Maintain authentication state using a React Context or a clean provider architecture.
Automatically attach the Firebase ID token as a Bearer token on every request made to the FastAPI backend.
Refresh tokens correctly when required.
Protect authenticated routes.
Redirect unauthenticated users to the login page.
Create reusable API utilities so future API calls automatically include authentication.
Follow modern Next.js App Router conventions.
Keep the authentication logic modular and avoid putting Firebase code inside page components.

After authentication, build the initial UI structure for the learning platform.